      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Vectors, Dot Products and Matrices",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Vectors and Matrices",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Vector== = ordered list of numbers: a point or direction in **n-D** space",
                "==Matrix== = 2-D grid of numbers, shape `(rows, cols)`",
                "A 3×2 matrix has 3 rows and 2 columns"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Dot Product and Cosine",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`a·b = Σ aᵢbᵢ = |a||b|cosθ`",
                "{green:Large positive}: same direction",
                "{red:Zero}: ==orthogonal== (perpendicular)"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Dot product",
                "Cosine similarity"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Formula",
                  "`Σ aᵢbᵢ`",
                  "`a·b / (|a||b|)`"
                ],
                [
                  "Length",
                  "**scales** with magnitude",
                  "**ignores** length"
                ],
                [
                  "Range",
                  "unbounded",
                  "==[-1, 1]=="
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Matrix Product",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`(m×n)(n×p) = (m×p)`",
                "==Inner dimensions must match==",
                "`AB ≠ BA` in general"
              ],
              "style": "number",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Common Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Operator",
                "Does",
                "Needs"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`*`",
                  "element-wise multiply",
                  "same shape"
                ],
                [
                  "`@`",
                  "matrix multiply",
                  "inner dims match"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Transpose flips the order",
              "text": "`(AB)ᵀ = BᵀAᵀ`, **not** `AᵀBᵀ`."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Derivatives and the Chain Rule",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Derivatives and the Chain Rule",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Derivative and Rules",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`f'(x)` = ==instantaneous rate of change==",
                "Geometrically: the ==slope of the tangent line== at x"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Function",
                "Derivative"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`xⁿ`",
                  "`n xⁿ⁻¹`"
                ],
                [
                  "`eˣ`",
                  "`eˣ`"
                ],
                [
                  "`ln x`",
                  "`1/x`"
                ],
                [
                  "Sum `u + v`",
                  "`u' + v'`"
                ],
                [
                  "Product `uv`",
                  "`u'v + uv'`"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Chain Rule",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`d/dx f(g(x)) = f'(g(x))·g'(x)`",
                "==Multiply local derivatives== along the path",
                "Backprop = chain rule, layer by layer"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "x",
                    "sub": "input",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "g(x)",
                    "sub": "local g'(x)",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "f(g(x))",
                    "sub": "local f'(g(x))",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Sigmoid and Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`σ(x) = 1/(1+e⁻ˣ)`, with `σ' = σ(1−σ)`",
                "==Max σ' = 0.25== (at x = 0)",
                "Many stacked layers multiply ≤0.25 factors: gradients {red:vanish}"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Don't drop the inner derivative",
              "text": "Differentiating only the outer function and forgetting ==g'(x)== is the classic error."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Gradients and Gradient Descent",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Gradients and Gradient Descent",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Gradient and Update Rule",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==∇f== = vector of **partial derivatives**",
                "Points toward {red:steepest increase}, so step {green:against} it",
                "Update: ==θ ← θ − η∇L(θ)==",
                "η = **learning rate** (step size)"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Batch vs SGD vs Mini-batch",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Samples per step",
                "Trait"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Batch",
                  "all data",
                  "stable, slow"
                ],
                [
                  "SGD",
                  "1",
                  "noisy, fast"
                ],
                [
                  "Mini-batch",
                  "32–256",
                  "**default**"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Example and Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "L = (w−3)², gradient ==2(w−3)==",
                "Start w=0, η=0.1: w moves to ==0.6=="
              ],
              "style": "number"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "w, eta = 0.0, 0.1",
                "grad = 2 * (w - 3)",
                "w = w - eta * grad",
                "print(round(w, 2))"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "output",
              "lines": [
                "0.6"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "η too large: **diverges**; too small: **crawls**",
                "Unscaled features: elongated valleys, slow zigzag",
                "Gradient 0 may be a saddle or local minimum, not global"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "red"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Probability, Bayes' Rule, Expectation and Variance",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Probability, Bayes' Rule, Expectation and Variance",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Probability Rules",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Probabilities lie in ==[0,1]== and sum to ==1== over all outcomes",
                "Conditional: `P(A|B) = P(A∩B) / P(B)`",
                "Independent events: `P(A∩B) = P(A)P(B)`"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Bayes' Rule",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`P(A|B) = P(B|A)P(A) / P(B)`",
                "==Posterior ∝ likelihood × prior==",
                "Test: sensitivity 99%, false positive 1%, prevalence 1%"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Numerator",
                    "sub": "0.99×0.01 = 0.0099",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Evidence P(+)",
                    "sub": "true + false positives: 0.0099 + 0.0099 = 0.0198",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Posterior",
                    "sub": "0.0099/0.0198 = 50%",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Expectation and Variance",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Formula"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Expectation",
                  "`E[X] = Σ x·P(x)`"
                ],
                [
                  "Linearity",
                  "`E[aX+bY] = aE[X] + bE[Y]`"
                ],
                [
                  "Variance",
                  "`Var(X) = E[X²] − (E[X])²`"
                ],
                [
                  "Std",
                  "`√Var(X)`"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Common Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Confusing `P(A|B)` with `P(B|A)`: ==base rate neglect==",
                "`Var(X+Y) = Var(X)+Var(Y)` needs X, Y ==uncorrelated==",
                "Independent implies uncorrelated, but uncorrelated does not imply independent"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Rare disease",
              "text": "A test with 99% sensitivity on a 1% base rate still gives only ==50%== P(disease|positive)."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Loss Functions",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Loss Functions",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What a Loss Is",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Loss = prediction error as ==one scalar==",
                "**Gradient descent** minimises it"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Loss",
                "Task",
                "Note"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "==MSE== = mean((y−ŷ)²)",
                  "regression",
                  "smooth, punishes outliers heavily"
                ],
                [
                  "==MAE==",
                  "regression",
                  "robust to outliers, non-smooth gradient at 0"
                ],
                [
                  "==BCE== = −[y·log p + (1−y)·log(1−p)]",
                  "binary",
                  "p from sigmoid"
                ],
                [
                  "==CCE== = −Σ yᵢ log pᵢ",
                  "multi-class",
                  "over softmax outputs"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Confident and Wrong",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Loss = −log(probability of the **true class**)",
                "True class 0.9 → ≈ 0.105; 0.1 → ≈ 2.30",
                "Confident wrong answers are {red:penalised heavily}"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "import math",
                "def ce(p):",
                "    return -math.log(max(p, 1e-12))",
                "print(round(ce(0.9), 3), round(ce(0.1), 2))"
              ],
              "note": "max() clips p so log(0) never happens"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "output",
              "lines": [
                "0.105 2.3"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Common Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "MSE for classification",
                "Softmax twice when the loss already includes it",
                "`log(0)` without clipping"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Pick the loss",
              "text": "==MSE== for regression, ==cross-entropy== for classification. Always clip before log."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
